UID:akshaya_tritiya-2027-05-09@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals\,birth-auspicious
DESCRIPTION:Why: a day set aside to start what should endure — learning\,
  giving\, household foundations — under the spring sun.\n\nStory: Akshay
 a Tritiya (Vaishakha Shukla Tritiya) is called 'never-diminishing' — tra
 ditionally favoured for beginnings\, charity and lasting vows.\nSource: Pu
 ranic akshaya lore\; regional muhurat custom\nWhy: a day set aside to star
 t what should endure — learning\, giving\, household foundations — und
 er the spring sun.\nModern angle: Muhurat timing itself is cultural\; char
 ity and intentional starts have known psychological benefits.\nEvidence: C
 ultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/re
 view/reasoning.html#muhurat-cultural\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-spec
 ific timing coming later.
