DESCRIPTION:Why: begin the season of vows by honouring the deity of thresho
 lds and careful starts.\n\nStory: Ganesh Chaturthi (Bhadrapada Shukla Chat
 urthi) installs Ganesha — remover of obstacles — at the doorway of new
  undertakings.\nSource: Ganesha Purana\; Mudgala Purana\nWhy: begin the se
 ason of vows by honouring the deity of thresholds and careful starts.\nMod
 ern angle: Community craft\, public art and shared vows\; cultural meaning
 .\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io
 /dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLocation basis: New 
 Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
